233	7	Verb TO BE - Complete Guide	Affirmative forms: I am, You are, He/She/It is, We are, They are	El verbo TO BE es el más importante en inglés. Se usa para:\n1. Identificar personas y cosas: "I am a student"\n2. Describir cualidades: "She is tall"\n3. Expresar estados: "We are happy"\n4. Indicar ubicación: "They are at home"\n5. Expresar edad: "He is 25 years old"\n6. Hablar del clima: "It is cold today"	I am a teacher. She is my friend. We are from Mexico.	\N	"She is beautiful. They are students."	"She are beautiful. \\u274c They is students. \\u274c"	"Confundir \\"is\\" con \\"are\\" seg\\u00fan el sujeto. Olvidar usar contracciones en habla informal."	En preguntas de confirmación (tag questions): "You are coming, aren't you?"	1	2026-02-04 04:56:29.645581
234	7	Verb TO BE - Complete Guide	Negative forms: am not, is not (isn't), are not (aren't)	Para formar negativos con TO BE:\n1. I am not (I'm not) - NUNCA "I amn't"\n2. He/She/It is not (isn't)\n3. You/We/They are not (aren't)\n\nUso de contracciones:\n- Informal: I'm not, he isn't, they aren't\n- Formal: I am not, he is not, they are not	I am not tired. She isn't here. We aren't ready.	\N	"He isn't a doctor. They aren't coming."	"He not is a doctor. \\u274c They not are coming. \\u274c"	"Poner \\"not\\" antes del verbo en lugar de despu\\u00e9s."	"I'm not" es la única forma - no existe "I amn't"	2	2026-02-04 04:56:29.648396
235	7	Verb TO BE - Complete Guide	Questions with TO BE: Am I...? Is he...? Are they...?	Para formar preguntas, invertimos el orden sujeto-verbo:\nAfirmativo: She is happy.\nPregunta: Is she happy?\n\nEstructura: BE + Subject + Complement + ?\n- Am I late?\n- Is he your brother?\n- Are they students?	Are you ready? Is this your book? Am I on time?	\N	"Is she a teacher? Are they from Spain?"	"She is a teacher? \\u274c (falta inversi\\u00f3n)"	"Olvidar invertir el verbo y sujeto en preguntas."	En preguntas indirectas no se invierte: "I wonder if she is happy"	3	2026-02-04 04:56:29.649763
236	8	Articles A/AN/THE - Complete Guide	A vs AN: Use "a" before consonant sounds, "an" before vowel sounds	La elección entre A y AN depende del SONIDO, no de la letra:\n\nUsa AN antes de sonidos vocálicos:\n- an apple, an elephant, an idea, an orange, an umbrella\n- an hour (la H es muda), an honest person\n- an MBA (se pronuncia "em-bi-ei")\n\nUsa A antes de sonidos consonánticos:\n- a book, a car, a dog\n- a university (suena "yu-"), a European (suena "yu-")\n- a one-way street (suena "wun")	I need an umbrella. She is a university student.	\N	"an hour, a hotel, an honest answer, a house"	"a hour \\u274c, an university \\u274c, a honest \\u274c"	"Guiarse por la letra en lugar del sonido."	Palabras que empiezan con "h" muda: an hour, an heir, an honor	1	2026-02-04 04:56:29.650822
237	8	Articles A/AN/THE - Complete Guide	THE - Definite article for specific things	Usa THE cuando:\n1. Algo es único: the sun, the moon, the Earth\n2. Ya mencionaste algo: "I saw a cat. The cat was black."\n3. Es específico por contexto: "Close the door" (sabemos cuál)\n4. Con superlativos: the best, the tallest\n5. Con ordinales: the first, the second\n6. Instrumentos musicales: play the piano\n7. Países plurales/unidos: the USA, the Netherlands\n\nNO uses THE con:\n- Nombres propios: Maria (no "the Maria")\n- Países singulares: Spain, Mexico, Japan\n- Comidas en general: I like pizza\n- Deportes: play football	The Eiffel Tower is in France. I love the ocean.	\N	"The moon is bright. She plays the guitar."	"I like the pizza. \\u274c (en general)"	"Usar \\"the\\" con nombres propios o cosas en general."	The + adjetivo = grupo de personas: the rich, the poor, the elderly	2	2026-02-04 04:56:29.65183
238	8	Articles A/AN/THE - Complete Guide	Zero Article - When to use no article	NO uses artículo con:\n1. Nombres propios: John, Paris, Microsoft\n2. Idiomas: I speak English\n3. Comidas/bebidas en general: I like coffee\n4. Deportes y juegos: play tennis, play chess\n5. Días y meses: on Monday, in January\n6. Transporte después de BY: by car, by plane\n7. Lugares con propósito específico:\n   - go to school (como estudiante)\n   - go to church (para rezar)\n   - go to bed (para dormir)\n\nCompara:\n- "He is in prison" (es prisionero)\n- "He is in the prison" (está visitando)	I go to school by bus. She speaks French.	\N	"Life is beautiful. I love music."	"The life is beautiful. \\u274c I love the music. \\u274c"	"Usar art\\u00edculos con conceptos abstractos generales."	Si es específico, usa THE: The music at the party was great.	3	2026-02-04 04:56:29.653008
249	12	Prepositions of Place - IN, ON, AT	AT for specific points: at the door, at the bus stop, at home	Usa AT para:\n1. Puntos específicos: at the door, at the corner\n2. Direcciones: at 123 Main Street\n3. Lugares comunes: at home, at work, at school\n4. Eventos: at a party, at a concert\n5. Edificios como puntos: at the bank, at the supermarket\n\nExpresiones:\n- at the top/bottom\n- at the end\n- at the beginning\n- at someone's house: at John's	Wait for me at the entrance. She's at work.	\N	"at the bus stop, at home, at the restaurant"	"in home \\u274c, on the bus stop \\u274c"	"Decir \\"in home\\" en lugar de \\"at home\\"."	in the office (dentro) vs at the office (el lugar en general)	3	2026-02-04 04:56:29.668982
