258	28	Past Continuous - Complete Guide	Past Simple vs Past Continuous: interrupted actions	Combinación de tiempos:\n\nWHEN + Past Simple (acción corta que interrumpe)\nWHILE + Past Continuous (acción larga de fondo)\n\nEstructura común:\n"I was doing X when Y happened"\n- Past Continuous = acción larga/de fondo\n- Past Simple = acción corta/interrupción\n\nEjemplos:\n- I was taking a shower when the phone rang.\n- While she was cooking, he arrived.\n- They were playing when it started to rain.\n\nDos acciones simultáneas (ambas largas):\n- While I was cooking, she was cleaning.	I was reading when the lights went out.	\N	"While I was walking, I saw an accident."	"While I walked, I was seeing an accident. \\u274c"	"Invertir los tiempos verbales."	Si ambas acciones son breves, usa Past Simple para ambas.	2	2026-02-04 04:56:29.682272
259	29	Comparatives and Superlatives - Complete Guide	Short adjectives (1 syllable): add -er/-est	Adjetivos cortos (1 sílaba):\n\nComparativo: adj + er + than\nSuperlativo: the + adj + est\n\nEjemplos:\n- tall → taller → the tallest\n- old → older → the oldest\n- fast → faster → the fastest\n\nReglas de ortografía:\n1. Terminados en -e: +r/+st (nice → nicer → nicest)\n2. CVC cortos: doblar + er/est (big → bigger → biggest)\n3. Terminados en -y: y → ier/iest (happy → happier → happiest)	She is taller than me. He is the tallest in class.	\N	"bigger, happier, the fastest, the nicest"	"more tall \\u274c, the most fast \\u274c, biger \\u274c"	"Usar more/most con adjetivos cortos u olvidar doblar consonantes."	Algunos de 2 sílabas pueden usar ambas formas: cleverer/more clever	1	2026-02-04 04:56:29.684097
