273	33	Present Perfect - Complete Guide	Use 2: Actions with present result (just, already, yet)	Present Perfect para acciones recientes con resultado presente:\n\nJUST = acabar de (reciente)\n- I have just finished. (acabo de terminar)\n- She's just arrived.\n\nALREADY = ya (antes de lo esperado, afirmativo)\n- I have already done it.\n- She's already left.\n\nYET = ya/todavía (preguntas y negativos, al final)\n- Have you finished yet? (¿Ya terminaste?)\n- I haven't eaten yet. (Todavía no he comido)\n\nPosición:\n- just/already: entre have y el participio\n- yet: al final de la oración	I've just woken up. Have you called her yet?	\N	"She has already eaten. They haven't arrived yet."	"I have finished just. \\u274c Have you yet called? \\u274c"	"Posici\\u00f3n incorrecta de just/already/yet."	Already puede ir al final para énfasis: You've finished already?!	3	2026-02-04 04:56:29.703514
274	33	Present Perfect - Complete Guide	Use 3: Unfinished time with FOR and SINCE	Present Perfect para situaciones que continúan:\n\nFOR + duración (cuánto tiempo)\n- I have lived here for 5 years.\n- She has worked here for 2 months.\n- for a long time, for ages, for centuries\n\nSINCE + punto de inicio (desde cuándo)\n- I have lived here since 2019.\n- She has worked here since January.\n- since yesterday, since I was a child\n\nPregunta: How long have you...?\n- How long have you lived here?\n- How long have you known him?\n\nCLAVE: La acción empezó en el pasado y continúa hasta ahora.	I have known her since 2015. He has been sick for a week.	\N	"for 3 hours, since Monday, since we met"	"I have lived here since 5 years. \\u274c for 2019 \\u274c"	"Confundir for/since o usar Past Simple."	It's been 5 years since I saw him. (= I haven't seen him for 5 years)	4	2026-02-04 04:56:29.704732
